  "chapter": 527,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 26 Chapter 527\n\n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 7353, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  insurance  law, in relation to encouraging\n        modernization of mutual  and  cooperative  insurance  companies'\n        information systems technology\"\n\n    APPROVED\n\n  This  bill  would  provide that if the expenses incurred by a domestic\nmutual insurer or cooperative property/casualty insurer in making a  new\ninformation technology system upgrade result in the statutory management\nexpenses  limit  being  exceeded,  then, upon the approval of the Super-\nintendent of the Department of Financial Services, that statutory  limit\nmay  be  temporarily raised to the amount necessary to encompass the new\nsystem upgrade for a period of six years.\n\n  The Legislature has agreed to a chapter amendment to reduce that peri-\nod from six years to  three  years  to  permit  additional  governmental\nreview  before  an  additional  three  year  period is provided. On that\nbasis, I am signing this bill.\n\n  The bill is approved.                       (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                                ______\n",
